A consumer catches up on the feed
A consumer is a name and a position. It asks the feed for the events after
its position, the feed reads a page from the tenant's database by keyset
cursor, and the page comes back with the position that follows it. The
consumer handles every event and only then records where it has reached, so a
consumer restored from its name alone resumes where it left off. Paging,
subscription, replication and catch-up are this one exchange.
